    "summary": "Rewrote the WReparse module (Model.ps1, PathSemantics.ps1, Walker.ps1, Audit.ps1, WReparse.psm1) to match docs/REPARSE-CONTRACT.md exactly.\n\nFixes: (1) canonical paths keep original casing and volume-root form, strip NT prefixes, and throw on unusable input; (2) Test-WReparseWithinRoot now compares on directory boundaries (root + '\\'), ordinal ignore-case, equal-to-root true; (3) Resolve-WReparseLinkTarget resolves relative targets against the link's own directory, never the process CWD or scan root, returning $null when unresolvable; (4) reparse classification uses FILE_ATTRIBUTE_REPARSE_POINT only, so hard links register as File; (5) Junction and SymbolicLink now map to distinct ReparseKind values; (6) State.Follow was hard-coded true — it now follows the -Follow switch, so without it no target is entered, Skipped equals the reparse-point count, and no cycle/broken_target errors are produced; with -Follow, broken_target (unresolvable/non-existent), cycle (target on the current branch",
